Whisper: the updater trusts Whisper's MAR signing certificates, not Mozilla's

What: the updater is built with Whisper's own MAR signing certificates (new files in
toolkit/mozapps/update/updater/ from gecko/overlay/) instead of Mozilla's release,
nightly or dep certificates: whisper_primary.der and whisper_secondary.der on every
channel except Whisper Canary's ("canary"), which trusts only whisper_canary.der.
Why: Whisper updates itself with Firefox's own updater, and an update is applied only
if its MAR carries a signature that one of these two certificates verifies. The
primary certificate signs releases; the secondary one is the rotation certificate,
whose key is kept apart, so Whisper can move to it without a manual reinstall.
Mozilla's MARs (and anything signed with another key) are refused. The canary has a
key of its own, used for every green build, so a canary MAR never installs on Whisper
and a Whisper MAR never on the canary.
Adapted from: the idea of Zen's scripts/mar_sign.sh (MPL-2.0), which copies its own
certificate over Mozilla's; here the build file points at Whisper's files instead.
---
diff --git a/toolkit/mozapps/update/updater/moz.build b/toolkit/mozapps/update/updater/moz.build
--- a/toolkit/mozapps/update/updater/moz.build
+++ b/toolkit/mozapps/update/updater/moz.build
@@ -107,25 +107,17 @@
 dep1_cert.script = "gen_cert_header.py:create_header"
 dep2_cert.script = "gen_cert_header.py:create_header"
 
-if CONFIG["MOZ_UPDATE_CHANNEL"] in ("beta", "release", "esr"):
-    primary_cert.inputs += ["release_primary.der"]
-    secondary_cert.inputs += ["release_secondary.der"]
-elif CONFIG["MOZ_UPDATE_CHANNEL"] in (
-    "nightly",
-    "aurora",
-    "nightly-elm",
-    "nightly-pine",
-    "nightly-cypress",
-    "nightly-profiling",
-    "nightly-oak",
-    "nightly-ux",
-    "nightly-larch",
-):
-    primary_cert.inputs += ["nightly_aurora_level3_primary.der"]
-    secondary_cert.inputs += ["nightly_aurora_level3_secondary.der"]
+# Whisper: the updater trusts only Whisper's own MAR signing certificates, never
+# Mozilla's. Whisper (release and every other channel) trusts whisper_primary.der,
+# which signs the releases, and whisper_secondary.der, the rotation certificate whose
+# key is kept apart. Whisper Canary trusts only whisper_canary.der (in both places), so
+# a canary MAR never installs on Whisper and a Whisper MAR never on the canary.
+if CONFIG["MOZ_UPDATE_CHANNEL"] == "canary":
+    primary_cert.inputs += ["whisper_canary.der"]
+    secondary_cert.inputs += ["whisper_canary.der"]
 else:
-    primary_cert.inputs += ["dep1.der"]
-    secondary_cert.inputs += ["dep2.der"]
+    primary_cert.inputs += ["whisper_primary.der"]
+    secondary_cert.inputs += ["whisper_secondary.der"]
 
 dep1_cert.inputs += ["dep1.der"]
 dep2_cert.inputs += ["dep2.der"]
